{"chunk_id": "73a22c56d35e", "text": "King Dasaratha, broken by Rama\u2019s exile, confesses to Queen Kaushalya the youthful sin that now returns as fate. While hunting by sound at the Sarayu river, he once mistook the filling of a water pot for an animal and shot an arrow, mortally wounding a young ascetic who had been gathering water for his blind parents. Dasaratha carried the water to the hermitage and revealed the tragedy. The grieving parents mourned over their son\u2019s body; the son briefly appeared in a celestial form and ascended to heaven. Before dying, the father cursed the king: he too would die from grief caused by separation from his son. Remembering this curse as Rama remains in exile, Dasaratha realizes destiny has arrived. Overwhelmed by remorse and longing to see Rama once more, he laments bitterly and finally dies in the night.\nKing Dasharatha recounts accidentally killing a hermit\u2019s son, recalls the curse of dying from grief for his own son, and finally dies mourning Rama\u2019s exile.\nThemes: karma and curse, parental grief, tragic destiny, confession and repentance, death of Dasharatha", "vector": [0.027257613837718964, -0.0035770623944699764, -0.006278177257627249, -0.017145918682217598, -0.02469971589744091, 0.022208428010344505, -0.01891779713332653, -0.013229135423898697, -0.031094463542103767, -0.0023713859263807535, 0.014468117617070675, 0.00865955464541912, -0.001821837155148387, 0.020942801609635353, -0.004935946315526962, 0.010804460383951664, 0.05038528889417648, -0.025578992441296577, 0.04417705163359642, -0.015174204483628273, 0.01421499252319336, 0.0005099978297948837, -0.005505478475242853, 0.014095091260969639, -0.021715499460697174, 0.005875174887478352, 0.007766954600811005, -0.02784379944205284, 0.016666313633322716, -0.017012694850564003, -0.0025245933793485165, -0.016479799523949623, 0.004279818385839462, -0.020329970866441727, -0.024073563516139984, 0.03631684184074402, -0.008519669994711876, -0.009825264103710651,